// Non-ASCII statements for the -c path. "你好" is 6 UTF-8 bytes, so the
// exit code pins the byte count: if the wide-argv decode mangled the
// payload (ANSI round-trip), the byte count changes and the exit code
// with it. A direct file run returns the same 6 — sources are read as
// UTF-8 either way.
string s = "你好";
return s.length();
